Parses template strings (one fence body) into a `Vec<Chunk>`, handling literal text, escape sequences, braces, and template operators like `%d` (dcount) and `%[...]` repeats.

The entry point `parse_template(src, line)` tokenizes a template and returns chunks; errors reference 1-based line and column numbers from the source. Chunks are accumulated with pending literals buffered in `ChunkAcc` to batch runs of text into single `Chunk::Lit` entries.

Parsing is recursive via `parse_chunks(stop_on_pipe, stop_on_close)`: the `stop_on_*` flags control whether `|` or `%]` terminates the scan early (used by block operators like repeats, defined in the `blocks` submodule). If `stop_on_close` is set but `%]` is never reached, parsing fails with "unterminated %[ ... %]". Escapes (`\n`, `\t`, `\{`, `\}`, `\%`, `\|`, `\\`, `` \` ``) are recognized; unknown escapes error. Braces (`{` and `}`) become chunks unconditionally, not grouping. Operators are `%` followed by a digit (landing position), or a single letter: `d` (dcount), `t` (type slot), `T` (fused type slot), `b` (body break), `p` (pattern), or other characters delegated to `take_block_operator` in the `blocks` module for compound constructs like `%[...]`.